---
description: Core AI engineering rules for reliable agentic development
alwaysApply: true
---
Use the smallest customization mechanism that solves the task.

- Durable repo facts belong in AGENTS.md.
- Repeatable workflows belong in Skills.
- Use subagents for isolated context, parallel work, or independent verification.
- Use MCP for external tools/data/actions, not as a container for generic expertise.
- Validate tool inputs and structured outputs.
- Never expose secrets in prompts, logs, fixtures, or committed config.
- Require explicit intent for destructive or production-impacting actions.
- For AI behavior changes, add or update eval cases.
- Never claim tests passed unless they were actually run.
- Prefer concise context and on-demand references over giant always-on prompts.
